      "user_id": "4826542193295360"
    },
    {
      "content": "A two bedroom typically, so with two bedroom apartments. When you're doing full packing it just really depends on like, just the amount of items that require, we were required to pack. We go by general rule of thumb that packing it will typically take roughly the same amount of time as moving does altogether when you can do an apartment. It's a little bit different though than it is the house. Specifically people sometimes people have more in an apartment in the house but typically people are going to have more in the house. So, roughly I would say for a three mover team still with a full service pack and move so we're packing everything wrapping, doing the full nine, I still with the free mover team, it typically takes roughly around eight hours seven it's like in the 7:00 to nine hour range especially when you're dealing with high-rise or high-rise and so on and so forth, it can become an extensive. Well, we will typically with two bedrooms we will typically split them up over two days cause we'll just send it to mover team and we'll have the two mover team come, the first day, they'll pack everything, they'll disassemble and prep everything that they can as well and then on day two since everything's already ready to go they just kind of show up and get it all knocked out the, it, it'll be a lot easier on the day two.",
